{contentTitle}\". Clear examples, important terms and statements, interesting facts, life applications.`",{"type":16,"value":118},"Connections",{"type":21,"value":120},"(contentTitle) => `Summary of the topic \"${contentTitle}\": key definitions, theorems, properties and examples of their use. All the most important things in a concise form!`",{"type":16,"value":122},"Key elements",{"type":16,"value":124},"Need to know",{"type":21,"value":126},"(contentTitle) => `Various problems with hints and answers on the topic \"${contentTitle}\". Interesting conditions, hints and detailed solutions. Turn knowledge into a skill!`",{"type":16,"value":128},"Depends on",{"type":16,"value":130},"Used by",{"type":16,"value":132},"Externals",{"m":134},"function m(number, one, few, includeNumber = true) {\n  const text = number === 1 ? one : few;\n  return includeNumber ? `${number} ${text}` : text;\n}",{"contentPath":136,"mainContent":137},"book/foundations/",{"fullId":5,"shortId":5,"contentRelativePath":138,"title":9,"bookTitle":9,"breadcrumbs":139,"description":140,"stats":141,"connections":148,"contributions":159,"type":8,"children":164},"01-foundations",[],"\n        All the foundational and most useful topics, formulas, and concepts on which all of mathematics is built.\n        The perfect starting point if you are a complete beginner in mathematics.\n        No prior knowledge required!\n        Everything is explained in a simple and understandable language.\n    ",{"materials":142,"elements":143},2,{"accent_term":144,"accent_statement":145,"accent_important":146,"problem":147},3,1,4,35,{"externals":149},[150],{"type":151,"items":152},"own",[153],{"type":154,"title":155,"info":156,"link":157,"reason":158},"web","LibreTexts Mathematics","An open and free online collection of mathematics educational materials.","https://math.libretexts.org/","A large amount of materials and many typical practice problems.",[160],{"contributorId":161,"name":162,"avatarUrl":163},"gwynerva","Peter Radko","/file/contributors/gwynerva/avatar.png",[165],{"type":166,"link":167,"title":168,"description":169,"stats":170},"group","/group/foundations/equations/","Equations","\n        Analysis of the most popular equations: elementary, quadratic, systems, etc.\n        You will understand why they need to be solved at all and how they can be used to describe processes in real life.\n        We will also consider nuances: transformations, domain restrictions, \"loss\" and appearance of \"extraneous\" roots, and many others.\n    ",{"materials":142,"elements":171},{"accent_term":144,"accent_statement":145,"accent_important":146,"problem":147},{"contributorsCount":145,"sponsorsCount":173},0,{"shortBookId":5,"frontNav":175},{"type":8,"shortId":5,"title":9,"flags":176,"link":11,"children":177},{},[178],{"type":166,"separator":179,"shortId":180,"title":168,"flags":181,"link":167,"children":182},true,"foundations/equations",{},[183,189],{"type":184,"shortId":185,"title":186,"flags":187,"link":188},"topic","foundations/equations/elementary","Elementary Equations",{},"/article/foundations/equations/elementary/",{"type":166,"separator":190,"shortId":191,"title":192,"flags":193,"link":194,"children":195},false,"foundations/equations/quadratic","Quadratic Equations",{},"/group/foundations/equations/quadratic/",[196],{"type":184,"shortId":197,"title":198,"flags":199,"link":200},"foundations/equations/quadratic/basics","Quadratic Equations Basics",{},"/article/foundations/equations/quadratic/basics/",1769364889884]